      "description": "Watch Qarabag vs Dynamo Kyiv highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. The UEFA Conference League stage was set for a massive clash on August 13, 2026 , as two ambitious sides looked to claim European glory. The atmosphere was electric as the referee blew the opening whistle for a night of intense tactical warfare and high-stakes football. Early Dominance from the Hosts Qarabag established their authority early in the match, controlling the tempo and forcing Dynamo Kyiv into a defensive posture. The breakthrough arrived in the 12th minute when Matheus Silva delivered a pinpoint pass to Jaly Mouaddib , who finished clinically to give the home side an early advantage. The goal sent the stadium into raptures and forced the visitors to rethink their approach under immediate pressure. As the first half progressed, Dynamo Kyiv struggled to maintain discipline while chasing the game. Their frustration boiled over in the form of yellow cards for Vladyslav Dubinchak in the 29th minute and Matviy Ponomarenko deep into first-half stoppage time. Despite their efforts to find an equalizer before the break, Qarabag remained organized and went into the interval with their lead intact. Sealing the Result The second half continued with the same intensity, as both teams fought for control of the midfield. Qarabag 's Badavi Huseynov received a caution in the 62nd minute as the game became increasingly physical. However, the hosts found the decisive second goal in the 69th minute. Elvin Jafarquliyev provided a brilliant assist for Oleksii Kashchuk , who calmly slotted the ball home to double the lead and put the result beyond much doubt. In the final twenty minutes, a flurry of substitutions altered the dynamic of the match. Qarabag introduced fresh legs including Musa Gurbanly and Samuel Lobato , while Dynamo Kyiv brought on Mykola Shaparenko and Vitaliy Buyalskyi in a late attempt to rescue a point. Despite ten minutes of added time, the home side held firm to secure a convincing victory and all three points in front of their passionate supporters."
