      "description": "Watch Dunajska Streda vs Twente highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 13, 2026. Dunajska Streda and Twente faced off in a high-stakes UEFA Conference League encounter on August 13, 2026. Both sides brought immense energy to the pitch in a fixture that promised plenty of tactical intrigue and offensive intent. Twente Take Control Early On The match began with Twente asserting their dominance away from home. It took only seven minutes for the deadlock to be broken when Max Bruns found the back of the net, clinical in his finish following a precise assist from Daouda Weidmann . This early goal set the tone for the first half, as the visitors remained disciplined and organized, frustrating the Dunajska Streda attack and heading into the break with a well-earned lead. At the start of the second half, Twente manager made decisive changes, introducing Marko Pjaca for Daan Rots . The substitution paid dividends almost immediately. In the 51st minute, Pjaca doubled the lead to 0-2, finishing off a slick move that seemed to put the game out of reach for the home side. A Spirited Fightback from the Hosts Refusing to back down, Dunajska Streda began a remarkable comeback that shifted the momentum entirely. In the 56th minute, Abdoulaye Gueye pulled one back after being set up by Zan Trontelj . The home crowd found its voice, and the pressure told again in the 66th minute. Klemen Nemanic converted an assist from Simen Kristiansen Jukleroed to level the score at 2-2, turning the game into a chaotic, end-to-end battle. As the clock ticked toward full time, the tension reached a breaking point. In the 88th minute, substitute Prince Owusu completed what looked to be a historic turnaround, scoring to give Dunajska Streda a 3-2 lead. The stadium erupted as the hosts appeared on the verge of a famous victory against their Dutch opponents. Stoppage Time Chaos With only seconds remaining in the four minutes of added time, the drama reached its peak. Twente pushed everyone forward in a final assault on the home goal. In the 94th minute, Marko Pjaca struck again, finding the net to silence the home fans and secure his second goal of the night. The referee blew the final whistle immediately after the restart, ending a classic 3-3 draw that left both sets of players and fans breathless."
