      "description": "Watch Apollon Limassol vs Brann highlights and goals from UEFA Europa Conference League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 11, 2026. The Apollon Limassol and Brann faced off in a pulsating UEFA Conference League encounter on August 11, 2026, where the stakes could not have been higher. Both teams pushed their physical limits in a match that provided constant shifts in momentum and kept the fans on the edge of their seats until the very end. Early Breakthrough and Physicality The match ignited with frantic energy, and it didn't take long for the deadlock to be broken. In the 16th minute, Brann took the lead as Kristall Mani Ingason found the back of the net, clinical in his finish after a superb delivery from Eggert Aron Gudmundsson . This early goal set a competitive tone, leading to a gritty first half filled with tactical fouls. Fredrik Pallesen Knudsen and Niklas Castro both saw yellow for Brann , while Alen Ozbolt was cautioned for Apollon Limassol as the teams battled for control heading into the break. Late Regulation Drama The second half remained a cagey affair until the closing stages when the match exploded into life. In the 86th minute, Apollon Limassol found their equalizer through Ivan Ljubic , who converted a cross from Morgan Brown to revitalize the home crowd. Just as the game seemed headed for a draw, Brann struck again in the 6th minute of stoppage time. Noah Holm scored what many thought was the winner following an assist by Vetle Dragsnes , leaving the score at 1-2 and pushing the tie into a dramatic extra-time period. Extra-Time Frenzy and Red Card The added 30 minutes began with a flurry of goals. Gaetan Weissbeck briefly pulled Apollon Limassol level again in the 92nd minute, but Brann responded almost immediately. Noah Holm secured his second of the night in the 95th minute thanks to Kristian Eriksen , before Eriksen himself turned scorer in the 105th minute to make it 2-4, set up once again by the influential Vetle Dragsnes . There was one final twist in the 118th minute when Kristall Mani Ingason was shown a second yellow card and sent off, leaving Brann to defend their lead with ten men. Despite the late dismissal, the visitors held firm to secure a remarkable victory in a contest that will be remembered for its relentless intensity."
